    <string name="chain_family_hint_evm">EVM-compatible chain. Only a chain ID is needed; every EVM chain shares one derivation path, so the same mnemonic yields the same address everywhere.</string>
    <string name="chain_family_hint_utxo">Bitcoin-style UTXO chain. The address shape is decided by the address type and three version bytes — getting them wrong makes the address unrecognisable.</string>
    <string name="chain_family_hint_tron">TRON. There is only one mainnet, so you rarely need to add it.</string>
    <string name="chain_family_hint_ed25519">ed25519 family (Solana / ICP / Monero). Each encodes addresses differently and derives keys differently — keep it consistent with the official implementation.</string>
    <string name="chain_family_hint_filecoin">Filecoin. Produces f1 (secp256k1) addresses by default; f3 (BLS) addresses can be recognised but are not generated.</string>
    <string name="chain_family_hint_chia">Chia. The address is bech32m over a BLS12-381 puzzle hash. This version supports watch-only addresses only, no mnemonic derivation.</string>

